  "result": "I withdrew span h5 (\"or in compliance with law\") as an `operator` gap rather than revising the record, so the law now goes to the operator. Nothing was run; the only output is `record.jsonl`.\n\n**Why the gate refused it:** the plan carried h5 as \"an emergency vehicle with its warning lamps or siren on is in the scene.\" That emergency vehicle has no link to the subject vehicle or to the intersection, which is why the gate returned `UNANCHORED_VARIABLE`.\n\n**Why I didn't just anchor it:** tying the emergency vehicle to the intersection or to a distance from the subject would add conditions the words don't state. It would also still be a neighbouring atom standing in for the law's actual condition, which the rules forbid. That condition is that *some* law requires the halt: yielding to an emergency vehicle, to a pedestrian, to a school bus, and so on. Composing another rule doesn't work either, because \"law\" names no particular rule.\n\n**What the withdrawal asks for:** an operator that decides whether some rule that applies to the subject at that moment can only be complied with by halting. It reuses the plan's own proposal, `Formula.haltRequired (subject)`. It lists `ru.emergency_vehicle`, `sig.warning_lamp`/`sig.siren` and `Formula.rule` as the nearest existing ids, each with the reason it can't carry the span.\n\nThe rest of the coder's rule (the other exceptions, the place condition and the halt itself) needed no change.",
